WEBVTT

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Otome</i>:

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.840
A maiden, sweet-smelling as a flower,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.970
a single bud blooming in a tranquil
garden, pure and dignified.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.230
Too shy to even speak of love or romance,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.480
she dares not allow herself
to dream of a kiss.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.900
Even so, she blooms again today--

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.030
seeking, ever seeking
happiness beyond the stars.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.550
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.080
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.040
"Episode 3"
"The Black Lily"

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:12.340
This is my <i>home </i>now!
You can't just drop by!

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.550
What do <i>you </i>know? <i>You're </i>dead.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.390
Perhaps I'll move here myself...

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:22.890
Miss?

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.020
We brought in the last of your bags!

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:30.310
Ah, thank you. Here's your tip:

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.940
ten yen for each of you.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:33.940
Is that enough?

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.110
It's outrageous!
Miss, we can't accept this!

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.700
Of course you can.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.240
You were a big help, bringing them
all the way here from the station.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:47.790
Th-Thank you very much!

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.880
I suppose you must be his betrothed.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.510
Y-Yes, I am. My name is Yuzuki.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.930
Hmm. Yuzuki-<i>san</i>...

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.890
It must be rough,
what with you being so little.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.350
What year of primary school are you in?

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.350
<i>P-Primary</i>?!

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:12.690
Ahem.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:19.190
As you can see, I'm a fine
upstanding adult woman of 14.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.400
What? 14?!

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.780
No way! You certainly don't look it.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:30.620
For one thing, no adult wears a
kimono with these shoulder tucks.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:35.960
Th-These are for when
I get taller someday!

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.960
"Someday"? When, exactly?

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:45.100
N-Next year! I'll be taller than
you next year--you'll see!

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.140
My! Isn't that <i>special</i>?

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:55.440
Tamako, Yuzu <i>is </i>older than you.
Show a little respect.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:00.190
What? But she's smaller than me,
and <i>I'm </i>12!

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:04.990
I can't show respect for someone
who still has her shoulder folds.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:06.530
<i>Twelve</i>?!

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.660
"12" "14"

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.660
I-I can't even argue with that...

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:15.830
My little sister: casually tossing
around comments

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:18.750
that land like a knife in the heart.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:26.760
Yuzuki-<i>san</i>, you really must rid yourself

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.890
of the embarrassing misconception
that you're an adult woman.

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:34.270
A-All right...

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.690
Now that's a <i>good </i>answer!

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:39.610
--She's one evil girl.
--There, there.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.950
Please use this room, Tamako-<i>san</i>.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.290
I don't want to. It's too small.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.050
I'll take this one.
It gets good sunlight, too.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:05.130
Understood. In that case...

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.430
I'll bring in your things.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.310
I'll have to air out the guest futon!

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:18.060
This is a little tea-sweet I've made.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.650
Please try it--if it's to your taste.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.690
My room is right next door,

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:25.110
so please let me know
if you need anything--

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.240
I don't!

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:34.580
I'm sorry. I never expected
to see <i>her </i>here.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.290
Not at all! The more, the merrier.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.250
"Merrier"?

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.050
You really are amazing.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.590
I am?

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:49.220
Tamako's not that easy to handle.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.890
She's the brightest of us siblings,

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:56.600
but you never really know
what she's thinking.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.980
For a long time,

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:00.650
she's been isolated, too--
in a different way.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:06.400
I thought attending girls' school
might have mellowed her,

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.070
but seeing her today... I wonder.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:13.490
Still, I'd like to be friends
with Tamako-<i>san</i>.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:16.160
I don't think that's possible.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.790
Oh! Tamako-<i>san</i>!

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:21.330
I was just about to ask you to join us.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.250
Since tonight's your
welcome party and all,

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.670
I'm really fired up about dinner!

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.010
How dumb.

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:28.970
Eh?

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:32.350
Would you kindly stop
such childish antics?

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:34.970
Tamako.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.440
Why exactly are you here?

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.060
To our family, I'm...

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.820
I'm already dead.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.440
Oh, that's right!

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:51.910
Seeing Tamaki and Tamayo ham it up
for their marriage prospects--

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.280
it was <i>so </i>entertaining!

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:58.160
All "Ah, my dearly beloved
little brother!"

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.540
and "If only I had died
in Tamahiko's stead!"

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.670
Even Father wiped away a tear!

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:09.800
It was hilarious!

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:18.810
I'd like to dine alone.
Please bring my dinner to my room.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.640
I'll pass on sharing
a table with my brother.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:27.650
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:30.150
Bring mine to my room, too.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:38.240
I know.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.910
Tamahiko hates me--I do know that much.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.340
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>. Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:50.510
You're not having breakfast?

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:52.680
I don't have an appetite.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.760
Not even a bite? But...

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:01.520
I'm sorry.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:07.110
It's hard, having Tamako
hit you with reality.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:09.190
And I thought I understood...

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:18.540
Say, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>,
will you go for a walk with me?

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.870
Huh?

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.620
There's something I'd like to show you.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.000
Actually, I--

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.380
But not far.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:34.970
Okay!

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:37.640
Come on--let's get going.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:38.890
This way!

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:44.850
"Destination" "House" "Village"

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:44.850
It's just a short climb
from where we are now.

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:51.860
What could possibly be
up a mountain like this?

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:53.950
You'll find out once we get there!

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.570
A river?

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.660
There's a spring higher up.
The water tastes great!

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.620
I had no idea.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:10.210
I've lived here for how many months now,

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.760
with such beautiful scenery all around me.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:20.430
It's up ahead. Please watch your step!

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:24.850
Here we are!

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.270
What a grand tree...

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:32.980
And?

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:37.490
Take a <i>really </i>good look inside!

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:38.490
Inside?

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.990
A little Inari statue!

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:45.160
Isn't it the cutest?

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.790
You almost never see tree-hollow shrines.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.750
Maybe it's the guardian
deity of this mountain.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:54.800
Isn't it wonderful?
Like some kind of fairy tale!

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.220
A fairy tale...

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:09.440
In this moment, the world itself
truly is like a fairy tale.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:16.320
You're right.
I think it was good, seeing this.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:19.820
I'm happy to see you're finally smiling.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:24.200
I always wanted to see this with you.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:27.830
I was wondering when
I should ask you to come.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:30.130
I'm so glad!

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:32.920
I must've had her worried...

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.210
...given that all I do is mope around.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.970
"siiigh"

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:40.090
Oh, right!

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.390
That spring is just over here.

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:54.730
It's cold--and delicious!

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:59.280
Go ahead and wet your whistle,
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.280
Sure.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.910
Okay.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:09.750
Here you go.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:13.130
Er, I-I don't think...

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.340
Put my mouth on Yuzu's hands?!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.050
It's really delicious.

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:31.390
It's good.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.520
That tickles...

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.690
"pop"

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.320
--Sorry.
--It's okay.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:48.240
Did you enjoy yourself?

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.250
Yeah.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:57.210
So did I. I enjoyed myself, too!

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:02.380
Let's come here again.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:03.390
Mmm.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:07.390
Oh! Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, look!

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.440
It's spring, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:21.070
I'd thought the cold,
dark winter would last forever.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:26.280
But before I knew it, a gust of wind

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.620
blew the darkness to who knows where.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:34.040
Yuzu was nothing less

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.460
than a spring storm.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.960
To 60 <i>monme </i>of sugar,

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:42.010
add 15 <i>monme </i>of wheat flour;

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:46.470
add two <i>gō </i>of milk and mix well.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:48.100
Reduce over a low flame

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:50.470
until it reaches a
glue-like consistency...

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.350
What are you making?

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.310
Milk caramels.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:13:00.530
What?! You can make those from scratch?

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:01.530
Yes.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.660
You certainly are brother and sister.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:12.120
Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>sometimes stands
there and watches, too.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:13.960
Stop that.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.710
Pour it into a shallow, buttered form,

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:19.880
and it will firm up in about an hour.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.170
What a hassle.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:26.630
I'm surprised you'd do
all that for someone else.

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:31.350
After all, weren't you sent here
against your will to settle a debt?

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:33.890
Deep inside, I'm sure you must hate it.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:36.390
No--not one bit.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:39.110
When I think I'd like
to do something for him,

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.980
my body moves on its own.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.360
That's all!

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.240
You're a strange one.

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.990
What?! Am I really?

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:50.870
Yes, you are.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.710
You made these? For me?

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:04.670
Yes--I thought you could
eat them while you read.

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:08.220
You didn't have to do that.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:12.560
For one thing, caramels are foreign
candy--I've never tried them.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.520
Then let's take this opportunity...

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.440
"Ah"!

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:22.150
F-Finger... in mouth...

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:25.070
I'm sorry...

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:28.740
Is it... is it good?

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:29.740
Huh?

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:35.080
Yeah. It's delicious.

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:37.750
It has a warm taste, somehow.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:39.750
What the--"a warm taste"?

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:42.130
It's just candy!

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:43.840
You can tell?

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.670
I put a lot of heart in each one!

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:47.970
Ha ha!

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.220
"Heart"?

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.340
Give me a break.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:51.590
Oh!

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.390
Please--have one, Tamako-<i>san</i>.

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.720
"Warm taste," my foot!

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.930
It's just a wad of sugar!

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:04.440
You're a couple of idiots, you know that?

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.860
Tamako-<i>san</i>...

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.260
Father...

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:36.720
Tamayo, um, she grabbed my book and, um--

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:40.020
I'm busy.

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:43.610
You there.

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:46.230
Here. Deal with Tamako, would you?

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.190
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:53.280
Well, now, Miss Tamako.
I'm at your service.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:56.160
No one will help me...

00:15:57.910 --> 00:16:00.410
There goes the Shima family's...

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:03.210
Her lofty height's matched
only by her attitude.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:07.750
Who would want a bride like <i>that</i>?

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:11.880
At home, at the girls' school...
everyone hates me.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:14.340
Everyone.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:35.530
My room is right next door,

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:37.660
so please let me know
if you need anything.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:39.830
Yuzuki-<i>sa</i>--

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.000
It's only thunder.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:49.130
What's wrong, Tamako-<i>san</i>?

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:51.840
N-N-Nothing!

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.800
I just need the lavatory.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:58.050
Oh, I see. You know
where it is, don't you?

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.970
Y-Yes...

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:02.480
No, I <i>don't</i>! Come with me!

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:06.690
This place is simply too dark!

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:10.690
All this thunder and lightning...
it's the worst!

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:13.570
You know, there <i>is </i>quite a lot of it.

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:15.820
I wonder if it'll strike nearby...

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.950
There it is!

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.660
That gave me a fright!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.970
Tamako-<i>san</i>! This way!

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:42.680
Into the tub! I'll get the fire going!

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.000
Why...?

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:15.050
Your hair is so beautiful, Tamako-<i>san</i>.
Like strands of silk.

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:18.430
Don't flatter me just to
get me to stop crying.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.640
It's not that.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:24.220
--See, I have wavy hair. You're lucky.
--Floofy floofy floofy floofy floof...

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:28.400
Why?

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.150
No one cares about anyone else's feelings.

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:36.030
If someone's holding you back,
cut them off--no mercy.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:40.160
But I've done and said
such awful things to you...

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:48.250
It's all right. Let's sleep here
together tonight.

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:56.380
I've never slept with
anyone like this before.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:58.130
Not even with family?

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:02.680
Coddling was forbidden from an early age.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:08.140
I thought I'd make fast friends
once I got to girls' school.

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:11.020
But they all just gossiped about me.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:13.940
It felt idiotic to keep going.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:18.860
When I took time off school,
Father was furious.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:21.950
"Do you want to end up like Tamahiko?"

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:29.500
Soon I couldn't stand
being at home, either,

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.540
and I came here.

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:36.420
So that's what happened.
You must have felt so alone.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:38.470
Not particularly.

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:42.430
If depending on others or seeking
their help meant only hurt,

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:45.010
I'd be better off living strong on my own.

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:49.430
If it were me...

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:51.980
If I were your big sister,

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:56.520
I wouldn't make such a darling
little sister feel lonely.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.280
Lies!

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:01.530
A little sister like me--big body,
bigger attitude?

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.570
There's nothing darling about me!

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:06.700
What if I called you "big sister"?
You'd hate that!

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:10.040
Of course I wouldn't.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.500
Eh?

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.210
It would make me very happy.

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.010
Really?

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.340
Yes.

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:23.800
So rest easy--and get some sleep.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:29.680
It's all right. This is spring thunder.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:32.640
It's telling us that spring is on its way.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.020
Spring...

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:41.900
♬ In the moonless sky I see them ♬

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:47.530
♬ Tiny lights that twinkle so ♬

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:53.580
♬ There, in those starry shadows... ♬

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:58.460
Wh-What <i>is </i>this?

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:01.800
What's going on?

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:03.880
Mix it up well, now!

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:06.220
Okay, sis!

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:08.470
Oh, I don't know about this...

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:11.890
Can I even <i>make </i>proper almond macarons?

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:14.520
I'm sure they'll come out delicious.

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:18.110
--Thanks, Yuzu!
--What could have happened
in a single night?!

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:19.690
Still...

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:21.070
All done!

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:24.820
So good!

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:31.830
I've never seen Tamako look so animated.

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:33.660
What are <i>you </i>looking at?

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:36.420
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, would you like one--

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:37.790
He can't have any.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:43.380
Kindly do not intrude upon
our maidens' moment!

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:46.050
What... what happened?

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:50.180
The spring thunder paid a visit--
and spring came to me, too.

00:22:03.780 --> 00:22:05.490
What happened?

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:41.210
It's going to be another hot one today,

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:43.080
but I'll dive in and do my best.

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:46.920
First I'll make breakfast, do the laundry,

00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:50.840
dust, clean the floors, and after that...
